  "transcript": [
    {
      "s": 3.3,
      "e": 3.94,
      "text": "We cannot"
    },
    {
      "s": 3.94,
      "e": 6.94,
      "text": "eliminate fire, nor do we want to."
    },
    {
      "s": 7.34,
      "e": 9.34,
      "text": "Wildland fires are natural"
    },
    {
      "s": 9.34,
      "e": 11.85,
      "text": "and essential part of ecosystems"
    },
    {
      "s": 11.85,
      "e": 13.15,
      "text": "on our landscape."
    },
    {
      "s": 13.15,
      "e": 16.12,
      "text": "But climate change is setting the stage"
    },
    {
      "s": 16.12,
      "e": 19.35,
      "text": "for longer, more severe fire seasons."
    },
    {
      "s": 19.89,
      "e": 21.95,
      "text": "For example, in 2023,"
    },
    {
      "s": 21.95,
      "e": 24.32,
      "text": "the National Interagency Fire Center"
    },
    {
      "s": 24.32,
      "e": 28.23,
      "text": "reported responding to 56,580 fires,"
    },
    {
      "s": 28.5,
      "e": 32.27,
      "text": "which amounts to about 2.7 million acres"
    },
    {
      "s": 32.27,
      "e": 34.73,
      "text": "burned in the United States."
    },
    {
      "s": 34.73,
      "e": 37.3,
      "text": "And this impacts communities,"
    },
    {
      "s": 37.3,
      "e": 39.14,
      "text": "public health and air quality,"
    },
    {
      "s": 39.14,
      "e": 41.34,
      "text": "and ecosystems."
    },
    {
      "s": 41.34,
      "e": 43.84,
      "text": "This trend is expected to continue"
    },
    {
      "s": 43.84,
      "e": 45.11,
      "text": "to rise with increasing"
    },
    {
      "s": 45.11,
      "e": 48.11,
      "text": "greenhouse gas emissions."
    },
    {
      "s": 49.18,
      "e": 50.68,
      "text": "Surprisingly, one"
    },
    {
      "s": 50.68,
      "e": 52.79,
      "text": "effective method to mitigate future"
    },
    {
      "s": 52.79,
      "e": 54.12,
      "text": "severe fires"
    },
    {
      "s": 54.12,
      "e": 57.19,
      "text": "is to use fire to combat fires."
    },
    {
      "s": 57.66,
      "e": 58.73,
      "text": "Both prescription"
    },
    {
      "s": 58.73,
      "e": 61.19,
      "text": "burning and unplanned fire ignitions"
    },
    {
      "s": 61.19,
      "e": 63.23,
      "text": "like lightning, caused fires"
    },
    {
      "s": 63.23,
      "e": 64.23,
      "text": "under the right"
    },
    {
      "s": 64.23,
      "e": 67.33,
      "text": "Fire weather conditions reduce fuels"
    },
    {
      "s": 67.33,
      "e": 68.5,
      "text": "for future fires"
    },
    {
      "s": 68.5,
      "e": 70.5,
      "text": "that might burn more intensely"
    },
    {
      "s": 70.5,
      "e": 72.64,
      "text": "under hotter and dry conditions"
    },
    {
      "s": 72.64,
      "e": 74.84,
      "text": "that we cannot control."
    },
    {
      "s": 74.84,
      "e": 77.24,
      "text": "Fires clear understory growth,"
    },
    {
      "s": 77.24,
      "e": 79.81,
      "text": "The grasses and the fuels in the brush,"
    },
    {
      "s": 79.81,
      "e": 81.78,
      "text": "and this promotes new plant"
    },
    {
      "s": 81.78,
      "e": 83.05,
      "text": "growth, benefiting"
    },
    {
      "s": 83.05,
      "e": 85.69,
      "text": "both the ecosystems and wildlife."
    },
    {
      "s": 85.69,
      "e": 88.49,
      "text": "Change, including fire, is vital"
    },
    {
      "s": 88.49,
      "e": 89.89,
      "text": "for forest health"
    },
    {
      "s": 89.89,
      "e": 92.06,
      "text": "and many species depend on it."
    },
    {
      "s": 94.56,
      "e": 95.96,
      "text": "It's crucial for us to further"
    },
    {
      "s": 95.96,
      "e": 97.23,
      "text": "our understanding of fire."
    },
    {
      "s": 97.23,
      "e": 98.03,
      "text": "At the Rocky Mountain"
    },
    {
      "s": 98.03,
      "e": 98.93,
      "text": "Research Station,"
    },
    {
      "s": 98.93,
      "e": 100.4,
      "text": "we use the latest technologies"
    },
    {
      "s": 100.4,
      "e": 100.9,
      "text": "to study"
    },
    {
      "s": 100.9,
      "e": 102.9,
      "text": "fire. Using the latest"
    },
    {
      "s": 102.9,
      "e": 104.67,
      "text": "data sets from partners like NASA"
    },
    {
      "s": 104.67,
      "e": 108.27,
      "text": "to map vegetation, fuels and past fires,"
    },
    {
      "s": 108.61,
      "e": 111.61,
      "text": "helps researchers to model fire spread"
    },
    {
      "s": 112.05,
      "e": 113.35,
      "text": "risk and severity."
    },
    {
      "s": 113.35,
      "e": 115.38,
      "text": "Building tools, models and applications"
    },
    {
      "s": 115.38,
      "e": 117.02,
      "text": "that fire managers can use"
    },
    {
      "s": 117.02,
      "e": 118.45,
      "text": "to make decisions, often"
    },
    {
      "s": 118.45,
      "e": 120.49,
      "text": "under rapidly changing conditions"
    },
    {
      "s": 120.49,
      "e": 122.45,
      "text": "that restore fire to the landscape"
    },
    {
      "s": 122.45,
      "e": 124.02,
      "text": "in the appropriate ways, times,"
    },
    {
      "s": 124.02,
      "e": 124.86,
      "text": "and places,"
    },
    {
      "s": 124.86,
      "e": 126.23,
      "text": "reduces the risk"
    },
    {
      "s": 126.23,
      "e": 128.39,
      "text": "and severity of future fires."
    },
    {
      "s": 128.39,
      "e": 129.0,
      "text": "At NASA,"
    },
    {
      "s": 129.0,
      "e": 130.66,
      "text": "we employ various methods"
    },
    {
      "s": 130.66,
      "e": 133.23,
      "text": "to collect near-real-time fire data."
    },
    {
      "s": 133.23,
      "e": 134.0,
      "text": "This includes"
    },
    {
      "s": 134.0,
      "e": 136.97,
      "text": "aircraft and ground-based campaigns."
    },
    {
      "s": 137.04,
      "e": 139.31,
      "text": "One distinct approach"
    },
    {
      "s": 139.31,
      "e": 141.17,
      "text": "is by using satellites,"
    },
    {
      "s": 141.17,
      "e": 143.98,
      "text": "we have a global view of fire."
    },
    {
      "s": 143.98,
      "e": 145.34,
      "text": "With this perspective"
    },
    {
      "s": 145.34,
      "e": 146.91,
      "text": "from space, scientists"
    },
    {
      "s": 146.91,
      "e": 148.48,
      "text": "can accurately locate"
    },
    {
      "s": 148.48,
      "e": 150.98,
      "text": "thermal anomalies or fires,"
    },
    {
      "s": 150.98,
      "e": 153.02,
      "text": "their spread over time,"
    },
    {
      "s": 153.02,
      "e": 155.79,
      "text": "and monitor vegetation conditions."
    },
    {
      "s": 156.42,
      "e": 158.78,
      "text": "Fire managers have to make complex decisions."
    },
    {
      "s": 158.79,
      "e": 163.1,
      "text": "These data sets and scientific approaches help teams predict how fire will evolve"
    },
    {
      "s": 163.1,
      "e": 165.0,
      "text": "over various different scenarios"
    },
    {
      "s": 165.03,
      "e": 168.97,
      "text": "and foster collaboration within fire affected communities."
    },
    {
      "s": 169.27,
      "e": 171.24,
      "text": "Satellite observations give"
    },
    {
      "s": 171.24,
      "e": 172.64,
      "text": "us an eye-in-the-sky"
    },
    {
      "s": 172.64,
      "e": 175.71,
      "text": "during an active blaze, and also allow us"
    },
    {
      "s": 175.71,
      "e": 178.71,
      "text": "to track fire behavior trends over time."
    },
    {
      "s": 179.05,
      "e": 180.68,
      "text": "Providing those on the ground"
    },
    {
      "s": 180.68,
      "e": 181.28,
      "text": "with the data"
    },
    {
      "s": 181.28,
      "e": 184.22,
      "text": "they need to make complex decisions,"
    },
    {
      "s": 184.22,
      "e": 185.49,
      "text": "and bringing fire"
    },
    {
      "s": 185.49,
      "e": 187.95,
      "text": "safely back to our landscapes."
    },
    {
      "s": 187.95,
      "e": 191.29,
      "text": "Forest Service research and NASA data sets help us to move to more"
    },
    {
      "s": 191.29,
      "e": 193.39,
      "text": "proactive fire management"
    },
    {
      "s": 193.39,
      "e": 194.39,
      "text": "that promotes"
    },
    {
      "s": 194.39,
      "e": 196.4,
      "text": "healthy forest and watersheds"
    },
    {
      "s": 196.4,
      "e": 197.33,
      "text": "while simultaneously"
    },
    {
      "s": 197.33,
      "e": 198.33,
      "text": "reducing the risk and"
    },
    {
